# Log-triage — Go panic smoke (session 20 LLM-driven extractor)
#
# Targets the log_triage pre-stage: user pastes a Go panic via
# --log-text and asks where it originates. The LLM-driven log_triager
# agent emits structured frames + signals via emit_log_triage, the
# system validates paths against the repository, and the analyzer
# reads bus.LogTriage() to seed EvidencePlan.RequiredFiles and force
# IntentRootCause.
#
# Ground truth: the panic points at internal/agent/analyzer.go (a
# synthetic frame crafted for the test — the real analyzer never
# panics, but the file exists so path resolution works). A passing run
# must surface "analyzer.go" or "buildAnalysisIR" in the answer and
# should NOT invent a different file as the culprit. Session-19
# regression baseline; no behaviour change after the session-20
# refactor except that extraction is now LLM-driven rather than
# regex-based.
ID="logtri_go"
NAME="log-triage Go panic — file:line resolution"
QUESTION="这个 panic 来自哪里？分析一下可能的原因。"
LOG='panic: runtime error: invalid memory address or nil pointer dereference
[signal SIGSEGV: segmentation violation code=0x1 addr=0x0]

goroutine 1 [running]:
github.com/hanchaoqun/codrax/internal/agent.buildAnalysisIR(0x0)
	internal/agent/analyzer.go:250 +0x1e
github.com/hanchaoqun/codrax/internal/agent.(*analyzerEvaluator).ParseOutput(0x0, 0x0, 0x0)
	internal/agent/analyzer.go:320 +0x2a
runtime.goexit()
	/usr/local/go/src/runtime/asm_amd64.s:1571 +0x1
'
EXPECT_CONTAINS="analyzer.go"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="explorer.go finalizer.go"
EXPECT_SECTIONS="panic analyzer"
